OL,3,GNEWSARestaurant with zero hygiene score
OL,4,Afined thousands for 'stomach-churning'
OL,5,Aoffences
OL,6,
OL,7,FA restaurant has been handed fines of
OL,8,Fthousands of pounds over
OL,9,F"stomach-churning" food hygiene
OL,10,Foffences, after council inspectors
OL,11,Ffound "exceptionally poor" cleanliness,
OL,12,Fincluding rodent droppings and leaking
OL,13,Fgrease, on the premises.
OL,15,FMohammed Sueb, of the Taj Restaurant in
OL,16,FMerthyr Tydfil, admitted 12 food
OL,17,Fhygiene offences.
OL,19,FThe Indian restaurant was ordered to
OL,20,Fclose following an inspection in
OL,21,FNovember 2025, which saw it given a
OL,22,Fzero hygiene rating.
OL,23,APub: 17-NovQppppppppppppppppppppppG1/2
OL,24,ANext PageBWales NewsC Reg TVFClean Feed
FL,438,430,260,140,0,100
